description:
We are seeking a strategic and hands\-on AI Manager to lead our dynamic team of engineers and scientists in building innovative AI solutions. The ideal candidate combines technical expertise with strong leadership skills, excels in cross\-functional collaboration, and is passionate about translating advanced AI capabilities into real\-world impact. As an AI Manager, you will guide the development of advanced data products and AI\-powered applications, while shaping the roadmap, processes, and talent that drive long\-term success. You will partner closely with stakeholders across Engineering, Data Science, Product, and Business teams to ensure scalable, production\-grade outcomes.





Now, if you were to come on board as our AI Manager, we’d ask you to do the following:


* Oversee the design, development, and deployment of scalable AI solutions across the organization;


* Provide strategic direction for AI initiatives while ensuring alignment with business objectives;


* Manage and mentor a multidisciplinary team of AI Engineers, ML Engineers, and Data Scientists;


* Lead technical architecture decisions, system design, and solution reviews;


* Foster a culture of engineering excellence, code quality, and continuous improvement;


* Collaborate with Product and Engineering leaders to scope features and prioritize development efforts;


* Stay informed on cutting\-edge AI advancements (e.g., LLMs, RAG, vector databases) and evaluate their practical application within the company;


* Establish best practices and frameworks for model development, MLOps, and scalable deployment;


* Present complex AI concepts and project outcomes to technical and non\-technical stakeholders.





Think you have what it takes to be our AI Manager? Here’s how we’ll know:


* 5\+ years of hands\-on experience delivering AI / data products, including at least 2 years in a leadership role;


* Deep technical expertise in areas such as Large Language Models (LLMs), Retrieval\-Augmented Generation (RAG), embeddings, and vector search;


* Strong software engineering fundamentals, including experience with Python and data science tools (NumPy, pandas, etc.);


* Proven track record of deploying AI models into production in cloud\-based environments (AWS, GCP, or Azure);


* Experience managing teams and projects in agile environments with strong prioritization skills;


* Familiarity with modern data platforms, database systems (SQL \& NoSQL), and RESTful APIs;


* Excellent communication and stakeholder management skills, with the ability to explain AI concepts to non\-technical audiences;


* A growth mindset, with a passion for mentoring, coaching, and developing high\-performing teams.




* Position Title: AI Manager
* Salary: 150,000\.00 \- 190,000\.00
* Employment Type: Full Time, Permanent
* Hybrid: 3 in Office Days




*In accordance with provincial legislation and our commitment to transparent hiring practices, the compensation range for this position is provided. Final compensation will be determined based on qualifications, experience, and internal equity. Canadian work experience is not required. Please note that artificial intelligence tools are utilized in the applicant screening process.*

We are looking for a skilled and motivated AI Engineer to join our forward\-thinking team. The ideal candidate is passionate about building cutting\-edge AI solutions, has a strong technical foundation, and excels in collaborative environments. As an AI Engineer, you will play a key role in designing, developing, and maintaining advanced data products and AI\-powered applications. You’ll work closely with cross\-functional teams—including Data Scientists, Analytics Engineers, Front\-End Developers, and ML Engineers—to deliver scalable and impactful solutions.





Now, if you were to come on board as our AI Engineer, we’d ask you to do the following:


* Develop and maintain scalable AI applications from concept to deployment;


* Collaborate with cross\-functional teams to define, design, and ship new features;


* Architect and implement efficient and reusable AI systems;


* Write clean, well\-documented, and maintainable code following best practices;


* Conduct code reviews, provide constructive feedback and mentor junior team members;


* Staying up\-to\-date with emerging AI technologies and industry trends to drive continuous improvement.





Think you have what it takes to be our AI Engineer? Here’s how we’ll know:


* Bachelor's degree in a STEM field (or equivalent experience);


* Strong experience with Large Language Models (LLMs), RAG, embeddings;


* 2\+ years of experience developing AI / data products in a hands\-on capacity;


* Proficiency in the modern data science stack (Python, NumPy, pandas);


* Strong cloud engineering skills and ample experience taking AI ideas to production;


* Experience with database systems (SQL and NoSQL) and data warehouses;


* Familiarity with RESTful APIs;


* Knowledge of version control systems (e.g., Git) and agile development methodologies;


* Excellent problem\-solving skills, attention to detail, and ability to work independently or in a team environment;


* Excellent written and verbal communication skills with experience in relaying complex concepts to non\-technical users.




* Position Title: AI Engineer
* Salary: 110,000\.00 \- 150,000\.00
* Employment Type: Full Time, Permanent
* Hybrid: 3 Days a Week \- Toronto/ Mississauga




*In accordance with provincial legislation and our commitment to transparent hiring practices, the compensation range for this position is provided. Final compensation will be determined based on qualifications, experience, and internal equity. Canadian work experience is not required. Please note that artificial intelligence tools are utilized in the applicant screening process.*

**Company Description**  

Launched in 2021 with a simple yet bold mission, Flink set out to give people back their most valuable resource: time. We didn't just join the quick commerce race, we defined its potential. By enabling customers to order from a curated selection of over 3,000 groceries and household essentials through our user\-centric app, we deliver what people need in minutes. We have fundamentally shifted the retail landscape across Germany and the Netherlands, while embedding sustainability into our core through an all\-electric delivery fleet, recyclable packaging, and a focus on reducing food waste.


Today, Flink has evolved from a disruptive startup into a resilient and sustainable powerhouse. In an industry defined by rapid change, we’ve mastered the balance of hyper\-efficiency and massive scale. With a network of around 160 hubs, we now bring the Flink experience to more than 22 million people, making us an integral part of the urban infrastructure. This impact is driven by a dedicated team of more than 10,000 colleagues, including a fully employed rider fleet that serves as the backbone of our operations. By generating over €550m in revenue in 2025, we have proven that our model is not only desirable but financially formidable.


Having built a proven foundation, we are now shifting from establishing our presence to accelerating our impact. Backed by prestigious partners like Prosus, Mubadala, Bond, DoorDash, Btomorrow Ventures and REWE, and fueled by fresh investment, we are entering our next major growth phase. We are thinking bigger, expanding our footprint, and refining every link in our value chain.


Our culture is defined by a shared bias for action and the commitment to being 1% better every day. We take ownership, stay close to the frontline, and support one another to ensure we never let another Flinker fail. We celebrate diversity and believe that our multicultural team is our greatest competitive advantage.


Are you ready to shape the future of quick commerce with us?


We are creating a brand\-new engineering domain: **Revenue Technology (RevTech)**. This domain will own the full commercial technology stack that powers how the items in our assortment are selected for each hub, how they are priced, how promotions and retail media campaigns are managed, and how product data flows through the organization. It sits alongside our Consumer Tech, Operations Tech, and Platform domains.  

As the **Associate Director of Engineering** for RevTech, you will be the founding engineering leader of this domain. Paired with our VP of Revenue, who leads the domain from the Product side, you will shape the technical vision, hire and grow the teams, and deliver the systems that directly drive Flink's gross profit and assortment relevance. This is a rare opportunity to build a domain from the ground up inside a company with real scale, real customers, and real urgency.

 **Job Description**  

* **Lead the RevTech engineering organization.** You will inherit a small group of engineers transferring from existing domains and grow it into a cohesive, high\-performing group across multiple product teams — including Assortment, Master Data \& ERP, Pricing \& Promotions, and Commercial Back\-office;
* **Partner with the VP of Revenue to own the domain roadmap.** Together you will prioritize across teams, balance build\-vs\-buy decisions, and ensure the engineering investment maps tightly to commercial outcomes like use\-case coverage, GP per category, and pricing automation;
* **Hire and develop engineering managers and engineers.** Several key roles — including an EM for Pricing \& Promotions, backend and frontend engineers, and a data scientist — are open and waiting for you to shape and fill. You will also manage the relationship with an external development partner building some of our systems, ensuring quality, architecture alignment, and a clean path to internalization;
* **Drive technical excellence in a greenfield\-meets\-brownfield context.** Some systems are being built from scratch; others are being transferred and evolved. You will define the technical strategy that brings coherence to this landscape — shared APIs, data contracts, service boundaries, and on\-call practices across small but critical teams;
* **Navigate a matrix organization.** Engineers functionally report into the CTO organization while being embedded in the RevTech domain. You will work closely with fellow Engineering Directors in Consumer Tech, Operations Tech, and Platform to maintain cross\-domain standards, coordinate shared services, and ensure a consistent engineering culture;
* **Champion AI and automation across the commercial stack.** RevTech's core mission is to optimize processes via intelligent systems — from data\-driven assortment engines and automated pricing to product data enrichment and demand forecasting. You will identify where AI and machine learning can create step\-change improvements, partner with our Data Science team to bring models into production, and foster a culture where the team continuously leverages AI to multiply its impact;
* **Represent engineering in commercial conversations.** RevTech sits at the intersection of technology, category management, and revenue strategy. You'll regularly engage with non\-technical stakeholders — Revenue, Marketing, Supply Chain — and translate their challenges into well\-scoped engineering problems.



**Qualifications**  

* You will bring 3\+ years of experience building multi\-platform applications (web, mobile \- iOS and Android, and backend);
* In Addition, you will have 2\+ years of experience as an engineering leader, mentoring and growing successful teams;
* A bias towards action, with the ability to make the tradeoffs between delivering outcomes and making things perfect;
* Significant experience in applying different architecture patterns like microservices, event\-driven systems, micro frontends, etc;
* A strong interest in the business problems we are solving, and empathy with our users;
* Adept at developing in one or more common programming languages such as Go, Kotlin, Swift, and/or JavaScript;
* Being a good listener, but can also effectively communicate their perspective;
* Highly self\-driven, professional personality with an aspiration to excel in your role;
* Capable of taking both the big picture and also getting into details when it is appropriate to do so;
* Business fluency in English.



**Additional Information**  

* A €1000 annual L\&D budget as well as individual coaching options to ensure you have plenty of opportunities to learn, grow and achieve your goals;
* 26 days of vacation, \+1 day every year up to a maximum of 30 days;
* A mobility budget of 35 EUR per month for Deutschland Ticket subsidy;
* A discount on your Urban Sports Club membership;
* Attractive company pension options;
* Unlimited access to an e\-learning and development platform, MyAcademy, including online German courses;
* Online discounts with Corporate Benefits and Future Bens;
* A cool discount off your personal Flink orders; be the first to test out new products!
* A modern and dog\-friendly office in the heart of Berlin \- lots of delicious lunch spots available within short walking distance.

*It is our commitment that every applicant will be evaluated according to their skills regardless of age, gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability status, or religion.*

